## Genuine report prerequisites

A-24H input331?338 requests VariableDictionary=IDF, Drawing=dxf:wireframe and
Constructions=Constructions. B-NOLIMIT-24H requests VariableDictionary=Regular.
Thus a Constructions-only selector or fabricated absence of other report input
would lose real first-scan side effects. General.cc1130?1469 reads all report
families once, in fixed family order and actual within-family input order, retains
all flags/options, then clears GetReportInput. Later scans reuse that cache.
Constructions and Materials selectors remain distinct; second alpha is read only
when Native NumNames>1. Existing RuntimeOutputRequest is an output-variable key/
name/frequency request, not this report-input/cache contract. SimulationModel owns
TypedModel/graph only; no raw report request survives there today.

Reuse RawModel/ordered_instances and existing compiler default/provenance machinery
for typed report preservation. Preserve default-applied strings and actual count/
blank/order facts. Retain genuine scan state, including drawing/dictionary flags,
not just InitCTFDoReport. Invalid surface-list input reaches warning/continue
helpers; their ordered messages and real backend effects require explicit coverage.

reportLayers writes genuine predefined string entries (column, object name,
material name) through the allocation/count/growth owner. Existing Rust heat-balance
reports are timestep ResultStore series, not that table. Native creates ten layer
columns; ordinary compiler admission also permits ten opaque layers. Standalone
Native eleven-layer input has an unchecked column-index risk when columns exist;
this audit introduces no clamp, extra column, artificial failure or wider admission.

reportTransferFunction consumes actual public coefficients, material IDs/names and
loader properties, outside/inside absorptances and outside roughness. Typed regular/
NoMass properties exist. NoMass thickness/conductivity/density/cp report zeros must
come from actual MaterialBase defaults, not guessed missing values. Coefficient
rows descend NumCTFTerms through zero; zero omits Flux. Exact Native F/G formatting,
widths, precision and headers are output behavior that needs a real EIO sink and
same-input verification. Source/QTF branches remain outside CON-01 no-source scope.
Fixed19 capacity remains an honest representation boundary; no truncation or clamp.

ShowFatalError writes actual error/display/summary messages, reads severe count/
last severe text, optionally updates/commits SQLite, calls an actual error callback,
then throws. ShowErrorMessage has output-header/input-processing/stream behavior;
DisplayString has message callbacks and kickoff/console conditions. A Rust typed
RuntimeError alone does not certify these backends. Optional backend scope must be
represented or explicitly separately pending, never replaced by an invocation marker.

